huntik%3Apage%3A3241"},{"target_title":"Suits","label":"Suits","target_id":"huntik:page:2050","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Suits","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2050"},{"target_title":"Unnamed Suit 040","label":"Unnamed Suit 040","target_id":"huntik:page:18801","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Unnamed_Suit_040","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A18801"},{"target_title":"Unnamed Suit 041","label":"Unnamed Suit 041","target_id":"huntik:page:26470","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Unnamed_Suit_041","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26470"}]},{"name":"height","value_wikitext":"5 feet 3 inches","value_text":"5 feet 3 inches","links":[]},{"name":"weight","value_wikitext":"130 pound","value_text":"130 pound","links":[]},{"name":"first","value_wikitext":"\"[[The Bookshop Hunter]]\"","value_text":"\"The Bookshop Hunter\"","links":[{"target_title":"The Bookshop Hunter","label":"The Bookshop Hunter","target_id":"huntik:page:4693","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Bookshop_Hunter","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4693"}]},{"name":"last","value_wikitext":"","value_text":"","links":[]}],"start":0,"end":460}],"sections":[{"heading":"History","level":2,"wikitext":"Nighlurker was invoked by [[Klaus]] to attack [[Lok Lambert]]. It helped [[Ammit Heart-Eater]] battle and defeat [[Metagolem]]. It then battle against Lok, [[Sophie]] and [[Dante]]'s [[Hoplite]] [[Titans]]. {{Source|The Bookshop Hunter}}\n\nKlaus's Nighlurker attacked Dante in the large battle in the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]]. Dante, however, kicked it into a wall. {{Source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}\n\n[[Rassimov]]'s [[Suits]] invoked Nighlurker to defeat [[Forest Queen Diana]] in a fight with [[Hippolyta]]. Nighlurker was summoned later on to attack the Huntik team but defeated by [[Metagolem]]. {{Source|Ladies' Choice}}\n\nA Nighlurker Titan was used by the [[Casterwill Hunters]] to ambush the Huntik team on their quest for [[Phoenix]]. Nighlurker fought with [[Caliban|Powerbonded Caliban]] but sacrificed by its [[Seeker]], in an attempt to get more energy, using [[Powerlock]]. {{Source|The Dead Magic Island}}\n\n[[Scarlet Byrne]] was attacked by a Nighlurker Titan during the great battle at the [[Blood Spiral Base]]. The Titan was pinned down and defeated by [[Montehue]]'s [[Fenris]]. {{Source|Lok and the Betrayer}}","text":"Nighlurker was invoked by Klaus to attack Lok Lambert. It helped Ammit Heart-Eater battle and defeat Metagolem. It then battle against Lok, Sophie and Dante's Hoplite Titans. [The Bookshop Hunter]\n\nKlaus's Nighlurker attacked Dante in the large battle in the Castle of Vlad Dracul. Dante, however, kicked it into a wall. [The Vampire Loses Its Fangs]\n\nRassimov's Suits invoked Nighlurker to defeat Forest Queen Diana in a fight with Hippolyta. Nighlurker was summoned later on to attack the Huntik team but defeated by Metagolem. [Ladies' Choice]\n\nA Nighlurker Titan was used by the Casterwill Hunters to ambush the Huntik team on their quest for Phoenix. Nighlurker fought with Powerbonded Caliban but sacrificed by its Seeker, in an attempt to get more energy, using Powerlock. [The Dead Magic Island]\n\nScarlet Byrne was attacked by a Nighlurker Titan during the great battle at the Blood Spiral Base. The Titan was pinned down and defeated by Montehue's Fenris. [Lok and the Betrayer]"},{"heading":"Abilities","level":2,"wikitext":"Using its '''Shadow Ambush''' ability, Nighlurker can hide in the shadows that surround it, and can then appear from any other shadow around. The large mouth where his abdomen would be possesses many sharp teeth with which is used to bite down on its enemies. Its saliva is said to contain deadly poison that can melt an enemy's armor like caramel. {{source|Huntik Magazine}}\n\n{{clear}}","text":"Using its Shadow Ambush ability, Nighlurker can hide in the shadows that surround it, and can then appear from any other shadow around. The large mouth where his abdomen would be possesses many sharp teeth with which is used to bite down on its enemies. Its saliva is said to contain deadly poison that can melt an enemy's armor like caramel. [Huntik Magazine]"},{"heading":"Gallery","level":2,"wikitext":"{{Gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\">\nNighlurker Amulet.jpg|Nighlurker's Amulet\nNighlurker Icon.jpg|Nighlurker's Icon\nNighlurker.jpg|Nighlurker\n</gallery>\n\n[[es:Acechador Nocturno]] [[it:Nighlurker]] [[pl:Pomiot Cienia]]\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Hecto-Titans]]\n[[Category:Blood Spiral Titans]]\n[[Category:Organization Titans]]\n[[Category:Warrior Titans]]\n[[Category:Average Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 1 Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 2 Titans]]\n{{Clear}}{{HectoBox}}","text":"Image caption: Nighlurker's Amulet\n\nImage caption: Nighlurker's Icon\n\nImage caption: Nighlurker\n\nes:Acechador Nocturno it:Nighlurker pl:Pomiot Cienia"}],"full_text":"Nighlurker is a creepy monster of a Titan that once served as a guardian of Egyptian tombs. It likes to ambush unsuspecting Seekers and drag them off into the darkness.\n\nHistory\n\nNighlurker was invoked by Klaus to attack Lok Lambert. It helped Ammit Heart-Eater battle and defeat Metagolem. It then battle against Lok, Sophie and Dante's Hoplite Titans. [The Bookshop Hunter]\n\nKlaus's Nighlurker attacked Dante in the large battle in the Castle of Vlad Dracul. Dante, however, kicked it into a wall. [The Vampire Loses Its Fangs]\n\nRassimov's Suits invoked Nighlurker to defeat Forest Queen Diana in a fight with Hippolyta. Nighlurker was summoned later on to attack the Huntik team but defeated by Metagolem. [Ladies' Choice]\n\nA Nighlurker Titan was used by the Casterwill Hunters to ambush the Huntik team on their quest for Phoenix. Nighlurker fought with Powerbonded Caliban but sacrificed by its Seeker, in an attempt to get more energy, using Powerlock. [The Dead Magic Island]\n\nScarlet Byrne was attacked by a Nighlurker Titan during the great battle at the Blood Spiral Base. The Titan was pinned down and defeated by Montehue's Fenris. [Lok and the Betrayer]\n\nAbilities\n\nUsing its Shadow Ambush ability, Nighlurker can hide in the shadows that surround it, and can then appear from any other shadow around. The large mouth where his abdomen would be possesses many sharp teeth with which is used to bite down on its enemies. Its saliva is said to contain deadly poison that can melt an enemy's armor like caramel. [Huntik Magazine]\n\nGallery\n\nImage caption: Nighlurker's Amulet\n\nImage caption: Nighlurker's Icon\n\nImage caption: Nighlurker\n\nes:Acechador Nocturno it:Nighlurker pl:Pomiot Cienia","raw_wikitext":"{{Infobox Titan\n| image           = File:Nighlurker.jpg\n| attack          = 4\n| defense         = 4\n| type            = [[Hecto-Titan]] Warrior\n| size            = Average\n| special ability = Shadow Ambush\n| users           = [[Casterwill Hunters]]<br>[[Klaus]] <br> [[Suits]] <br>[[Unnamed Suit 040]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 041]]\n| height          = 5 feet 3 inches\n| weight          = 130 pound\n| first           = \"[[The Bookshop Hunter]]\"\n| last            =\n}}\n'''Nighlurker''' is a creepy monster of a [[Titan]] that once served as a guardian of Egyptian tombs. It likes to ambush unsuspecting [[Seekers]] and drag them off into the darkness.\n\n== History ==\nNighlurker was invoked by [[Klaus]] to attack [[Lok Lambert]]. It helped [[Ammit Heart-Eater]] battle and defeat [[Metagolem]]. It then battle against Lok, [[Sophie]] and [[Dante]]'s [[Hoplite]] [[Titans]]. {{Source|The Bookshop Hunter}}\n\nKlaus's Nighlurker attacked Dante in the large battle in the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]]. Dante, however, kicked it into a wall. {{Source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}\n\n[[Rassimov]]'s [[Suits]] invoked Nighlurker to defeat [[Forest Queen Diana]] in a fight with [[Hippolyta]]. Nighlurker was summoned later on to attack the Huntik team but defeated by [[Metagolem]]. {{Source|Ladies' Choice}}\n\nA Nighlurker Titan was used by the [[Casterwill Hunters]] to ambush the Huntik team on their quest for [[Phoenix]]. Nighlurker fought with [[Caliban|Powerbonded Caliban]] but sacrificed by its [[Seeker]], in an attempt to get more energy, using [[Powerlock]]. {{Source|The Dead Magic Island}}\n\n[[Scarlet Byrne]] was attacked by a Nighlurker Titan during the great battle at the [[Blood Spiral Base]]. The Titan was pinned down and defeated by [[Montehue]]'s [[Fenris]]. {{Source|Lok and the Betrayer}}\n\n== Abilities ==\nUsing its '''Shadow Ambush''' ability, Nighlurker can hide in the shadows that surround it, and can then appear from any other shadow around. The large mouth where his abdomen would be possesses many sharp teeth with which is used to bite down on its enemies. Its saliva is said to contain deadly poison that can melt an enemy's armor like caramel. {{source|Huntik Magazine}}\n\n{{clear}}\n\n== Gallery ==\n{{Gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\">\nNighlurker Amulet.jpg|Nighlurker's Amulet\nNighlurker Icon.jpg|Nighlurker's Icon\nNighlurker.jpg|Nighlurker\n</gallery>\n\n[[es:Acechador Nocturno]] [[it:Nighlurker]] [[pl:Pomiot Cienia]]\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Hecto-Titans]]\n[[Category:Blood Spiral Titans]]\n[[Category:Organization Titans]]\n[[Category:Warrior Titans]]\n[[Category:Average Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 1 Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 2 Titans]]\n{{Clear}}{{HectoBox}}","categories":["Average Titans","Blood Spiral Titans","Hecto-Titans","Organization Titans","Season 1 Titans","Season 2 Titans","Titans","Warrior Titans"],"links":[{"target_id":"huntik:page:2832","status":"resolved","target_title":"Hecto-Titan","label":"Hecto-Titan","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Hecto-Titan","href":"#/categories?name=Hecto-Titans"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:9603","status":"resolved","target_title":"Casterwill Hunters","label":"Casterwill Hunters","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Casterwill_Hunters","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A9603"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:3241","status":"resolved","target_title":"Klaus","label":"Klaus","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Klaus","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3241"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2050","status":"resolved","target_title":"Suits","label":"Suits","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Suits","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2050"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:18801","status":"resolved","target_title":"Unnamed Suit 040","label":"Unnamed Suit 040","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Unnamed_Suit_040","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A18801"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:26470","status":"resolved","target_title":"Unnamed Suit 041","label":"Unnamed Suit 041","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Unnamed_Suit_041","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26470"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:4693","status":"resolved","target_title":"The Bookshop Hunter","label":"The Bookshop Hunter","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Bookshop_Hunter","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4693"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2010","status":"resolved","target_title":"Titan","label":"Titan","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Titan","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2010"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:1997","status":"resolved","target_title":"Seekers","label":"Seekers","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Seekers","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A1997"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:3241","status":"resolved","target_title":"Klaus","label":"Klaus","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Klaus","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3241"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:1983","status":"resolved","target_title":"Lok Lambert","label":"Lok Lambert","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Lok_Lambert","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A1983"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:3356","status":"resolved","target_title":"Ammit Heart-Eater","label":"Ammit Heart-Eater","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Ammit_Heart-Eater","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3356"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2143","status":"resolved","target_title":"Metagolem","label":"Metagolem","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Metagolem","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2143"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2041","status":"resolved","target_title":"Sophie","label":"Sophie","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Sophie","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2041"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2006","status":"resolved","target_title":"Dante","label":"Dante","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Dante","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2006"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2899","status":"resolved","target_title":"Hoplite","label":"Hoplite","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Hoplite","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2899"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2010","status":"resolved","target_title":"Titans","label":"Titans","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Titans","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2010"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:3921","status":"resolved","target_title":"Castle of Vlad Dracul","label":"Castle of Vlad Dracul","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Castle_of_Vlad_Dracul","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3921"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2090","status":"resolved","target_title":"Rassimov","label":"Rassimov","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Rassimov","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2090"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2050","status":"resolved","target_title":"Suits","label":"Suits","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Suits","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2050"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:3084","status":"resolved","target_title":"Forest Queen Diana","label":"Forest Queen Diana","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Forest_Queen_Diana","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3084"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:3497","status":"resolved","target_title":"Hippolyta","label":"Hippolyta","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Hippolyta","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3497"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:214